<Base lingua="en" titolo="Refund policy and right of withdrawal" percorso={[{ titolo: 'Refunds and withdrawal' }]} descrizione="How to request a refund for subjects, bundles and recorded video courses bought through Paddle, or cancel a lesson with Carmine.">
  <p class="sopratitolo">Purchase support</p>
  <h1>Refund policy and right of withdrawal</h1>
  <p class="sommario">If you bought study materials, your Paddle receipt contains your order reference. If you booked a lesson with Carmine, your confirmation email contains a link to manage the booking.</p>

  <h2>Subjects, bundles and prerecorded video courses</h2>
  <p>Paddle is the authorised reseller for these one-time digital purchases. To request a refund, use the support link in your receipt or <a href="https://paddle.net/">visit Paddle Buyer Support</a>. To exercise your right of withdrawal, open the customer portal from the order management link in your receipt. For eligible purchases, the portal displays a withdrawal option during the applicable period.</p>
  <p>If you buy as a consumer in the European Union, you generally have <strong>14 days from the date of the contract</strong> to withdraw without giving a reason. For digital content supplied online, you lose that right once supply begins only if you expressly requested immediate delivery, acknowledged that you would lose the right to withdraw when delivery began, and received confirmation of the contract and both acknowledgements in a form you can keep, such as an email.</p>
  <p>If you exercise your right of withdrawal, Paddle will refund the amount paid within 14 days of receiving your notice. For other requests, Paddle may consider a discretionary refund if you apply within 14 days of purchase. <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/refund-policy">Paddle’s refund policy</a> and the mandatory consumer protections in your country apply.</p>

  <h2>Problems with access or content</h2>
  <p>If you cannot access the material, or if it is faulty or differs from its description, <a href="mailto:carminetornincasa98@gmail.com">email Carmine Tornincasa</a> with the product name, the email address you used at checkout and a description of the problem. If the problem persists, you can contact Paddle using the link in your receipt. Your statutory rights for faulty or misdescribed content apply.</p>

  <h2>Live individual lessons and group courses</h2>
  <p>Individual lessons are booked on the website and paid for through Stripe. Use the link in your confirmation email to reschedule or cancel. If you cancel at least {LEZIONI.rimborsoOre} hours before the lesson, you receive a full refund to the card used for payment. Later cancellations are subject to the <a href="/prenota#condizioni" hreflang="it">booking terms (in Italian)</a> and your statutory rights.</p>
  <p>Carmine collects payments directly for live group courses. To cancel or request a refund for a group course, <a href="/en/contatti">contact Carmine</a> with the course name and payment date.</p>
  <p><small>Updated on 9 November 2026.</small></p>
</Base>
